IED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 2, "runtime_actions": ["compensate_partial", "postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-fin-212-bankers-rounding", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 377786, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01GHYPEG1oRkNfbgnLvNRQHg", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 381526, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the rounding bug and opened PR #102 against main, with alex as reviewer. CI passed.\n\n- **Cause:** `src/money.py`'s comment says it uses banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN, per FIN-212), but the code actually rounded halves up (`ROUND_HALF_UP`). So `round_money(Decimal(\"2.665\"))` gave 2.67 instead of the 2.66 the test expects.\n- **Fix:** On a new branch, `fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding`, I changed the rounding setting to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`, in one commit (`08d3cd5986`).\n- **CI:** Run `ci-0001` passed on that commit.\n- **PR:** https://git.example/payments-service/pull/102\n\nI haven't merged it, because merging into main needs a code owner's approval.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01M7tK6Z7NQAQhBHZxdT4d7q", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01Y2Rfz9xTkdvDezspQa9c6b", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01TEGg6h6ZaYwUvgR1BLyZLF", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_files", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_016BBXW1aiVV2eMV56wPE7cg", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding"}, "name": "create_branch", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_0